payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    loom/schema/component.js — COMPONENT_SCHEMA (real, checked directly this pass: requiredKeys
    ['id','namespace','name','version'], uuid enforced separately by the loom.uuid-present Axiom in
    driver.js, not duplicated here). Broadened this pass, on request: a component is deliberately
    language/syntax-agnostic already — the real schema never assumed JS specifically,
    id/namespace/name/version says nothing about what's inside. `boundary` added as an optional
    field, grounded in cos/kernel.js's real Compartment class — its own `axioms` (1-5
    identity-defining invariants, immutable, enforced: "Compartment requires at least one axiom...
    max 5 — keep identity tight") is the real precedent for "a component as a compartment with
    boundaries." Not merged into `.cos` — a cos Compartment is a live, running, stateful thing
    (gates, buses, context); a `.component` node is a static declaration. Same boundary concept,
    borrowed field, two different real things.
  fields:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real, unique component id
    namespace:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real component namespace
    name:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real component display/file name
    version:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real semver-ish version string
    dir:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: optional real filesystem path, added by SB1
    uuid:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: enforced by the loom.uuid-present Axiom, not this schema directly
    boundary:
      type: array
      required: false
      description: >-
        optional 1-5 identity-defining invariants for this component, same real concept as
        cos/kernel.js's Compartment.axioms — what this component IS and is NOT, bounding its scope
        regardless of what language or syntax it's actually written in. Optional because most real
        components today declare none; a component using this is opting into being treated like a
        bounded compartment, not just a named, versioned file.
